+## Evidence (one line per box, same order)
+
+Build `13f0c2b` (WP-12), `?test=1&mode=museum`, captured with the `@capture` spec into `out/wp12/` (scratch, regenerated by the WP-12 commands).
+
+1. Thumbnail `out/wp12/verafin-thumb.png` (and `out/wp12/high/verafin-thumb.png`): one silhouette on the walnut tray, a light frosted column with the dark brass collar and cartridges at mid height, beside a bright stepped block of bars rising toward the back row; strong value contrast against the case and wall.
+2. Only the bar InstancedMesh is written (`engine.ts` `createRefreshDriver`); with `&idle=1` and motion on, every changed pixel over 16 s lies in the grid region (canvas x 706 to 791, y 492 to 544 at 1440 x 900); the column, core, collar and cartridges never change. Manifest `motion: 'slow'`.
+3. Three cartridges (`CARTRIDGE.azimuthsDeg` 90, 210, 330), each spanning radius 0.07 (the glass) to 0.14 and passing through the collar tube (0.070 to 0.086, y 0.292 to 0.308), unit-tested in `engine.test.ts`; collar inner edge on the glass; conduit, column and bars stand on the tray top (y 0.055); the tray sits on the 2.5 cm slot reveal and reads grounded by the contact-shadow line (`out/wp12/high/verafin-desktop.png`).
+4. All 36 bars use the one bone `ceramic`, never tinted or highlighted; heights come from a seeded level, trend and back-row rise with per-bar variation (a stepped block, no outlier); no icon, magnifier, particles or streams anywhere in the code or the shots.
+5. No Text, Html or texture in the component; the shots show no label, number or text on the object.
+6. `stats().exhibits.verafin` on desktop and pixel7: `inBounds: true`, 2,732 triangles (budget 4,000, limit 20,000), 9 draw calls.
+7. `ReportingEngine.tsx` uses `useMaterial` for walnut, frostedGlass, brass and ceramic and `useMaterialInstance('accentGlow')` for the core (static emissive 0.35); nothing else.
+8. `?test=1`: `exhibit-contract.spec.ts` two canvas shots 3 s apart are identical (desktop and pixel7). Reduced motion (`reducedMotion: 'reduce'` with `&idle=1`, so the clock may run): canvas shots at 0 s, 3 s and 10 s are byte-identical, past the 8 s refresh.
 
